## Why This Is Asked

This question tests understanding of augmented binary search trees to support order statistics—a fundamental data structures concept.

## Key Concepts

- **Augmented BST/Treap**: Each node stores value, count (for duplicates), and subtreeSize
- **Order statistics**: getKthSmallest navigates using left subtree size and node counts
- **Duplicate handling**: Multiple identical values stored in a single node with a count field
- **Rebalancing**: Operations maintain O(log n) time via rotations or split/merge

## Code Example

```javascript
class Node {
  constructor(v) {
    this.v = v;
    this.c = 1;      // count of this value
    this.sz = 1;     // subtree size
    this.l = null;
    this.r = null;
    this.p = null;  // priority for treap
  }

  upd() {
    this.sz = (this.l?.sz || 0) + (this.r?.sz || 0) + this.c;
  }
}

function kth(node, k) {
  if (!node) return null;
  const leftSize = node.l?.sz || 0;
  if (k <= leftSize) return kth(node.l, k);
  if (k <= leftSize + node.c) return node.v;
  return kth(node.r, k - leftSize - node.c);
}
```

## Time Complexity

- Insert: O(log n)
- EraseOne: O(log n)
- GetKthSmallest: O(log n)

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design a mutable deque with constant-time min/max queries, a common interview pattern for surface-level data-structure mastery.

## Key Concepts
- Deque operations and invariants
- Two-stack technique for amortized efficiency
- Maintaining per-element min/max for O(1) queries
- Edge-case handling (empty, duplicates)

## Code Example
```javascript
class MinMaxDeque {
  constructor() {
    this.front = [];
    this.back = [];
  }
  pushFront(x) {
    const last = this.front[this.front.length - 1];
    const mn = last ? Math.min(x, last.min) : x;
    const mx = last ? Math.max(x, last.max) : x;
    this.front.push({ v: x, min: mn, max: mx });
  }
  pushBack(x) {
    const last = this.back[this.back.length - 1];
    const mn = last ? Math.min(x, last.min) : x;
    const mx = last ? Math.max(x, last.max) : x;
    this.back.push({ v: x, min: mn, max: mx });
  }
  popFront() {
    if (this.front.length === 0) {
      while (this.back.length) this.pushFront(this.back.pop().v);
    }
    if (this.front.length === 0) throw new Error('empty');
    return this.front.pop().v;
  }
  popBack() {
    if (this.back.length === 0) {
      while (this.front.length) this.pushBack(this.front.pop().v);
    }
    if (this.back.length === 0) throw new Error('empty');
    return this.back.pop().v;
  }
  getMin() {
    if (this.front.length === 0 && this.back.length === 0) throw new Error('empty');
    let mn = null;
    if (this.front.length) mn = this.front[this.front.length - 1].min;
    if (this.back.length) {
      const bmin = this.back[this.back.length - 1].min;
      mn = mn === null ? bmin : Math.min(mn, bmin);
    }
    return mn;
  }
  getMax() {
    if (this.front.length === 0 && this.back.length === 0) throw new Error('empty');
    let mx = null;
    if (this.front.length) mx = this.front[this.front.length - 1].max;
    if (this.back.length) {
      const bmax = this.back[this.back.length - 1].max;
      mx = mx === null ? bmax : Math.max(mx, bmax);
    }
    return mx;
  }
}
```

